Only library sources are vendored: none of these directories contains the
programs/ or tests/ trees that carry GPL terms in some of the upstream
projects, so no GPL-licensed file is compiled into 7-ZSTar.

Assets taken from 7-Zip's binary release, which is the only place upstream
publishes them - they are not in its source tree. Their terms are the ones
stated in that package's own licence file, reproduced here as LICENSE-7-Zip.txt:
"All other files: the GNU LGPL".

- Lang/ - 7-Zip's translations. Every string is upstream's work apart from the
  product name, which is rewritten to 7-ZSTar (Lang/UPSTREAM.md).
- Help/7-zip.chm - 7-Zip's compiled help file, byte-identical to upstream's
  (Help/UPSTREAM.md).
- LICENSE-7-Zip.txt - upstream's licence statement itself, byte-identical.
  It is installed rather than merely cited because it says: "Redistributions
  in binary form must reproduce related license information from this file."

